0-axylo-canvas-vs-axylo-svg-e741` | complete |\n   588\t| first-3x120-uplot-vs-canvas | `20261118T023022Z-first-3x120-uplot-vs-axylo-canvas-e472` | complete |\n   589\t| first-3x120-uplot-vs-svg | `20261118T023053Z-first-3x120-uplot-vs-axylo-svg-7ee1` | complete |\n   590\t| first-1x10000-canvas-vs-svg | `20261118T023123Z-first-1x10000-axylo-canvas-vs-axylo-svg-5eaa` | complete |\n   591\t| first-1x10000-uplot-vs-canvas | `20261118T023155Z-first-1x10000-uplot-vs-axylo-canvas-f92c` | complete |\n   592\t| first-1x10000-uplot-vs-svg | `20261118T023225Z-first-1x10000-uplot-vs-axylo-svg-a264` | complete |\n   593\t| first-1x100000-canvas-vs-svg | `20261118T023256Z-first-1x100000-axylo-canvas-vs-axylo-svg-7ca9` | complete |\n   594\t| first-1x100000-uplot-vs-canvas | `20261118T023328Z-first-1x100000-uplot-vs-axylo-canvas-6583` | complete |\n   595\t| first-1x100000-uplot-vs-svg | `20261118T023400Z-first-1x100000-uplot-vs-axylo-svg-e9b6` | complete |\n   596\t| first-1x100000gaps-canvas-vs-svg | `20261118T023431Z-first-1x100000-gaps-axylo-canvas-vs-axylo-svg-0fe2` | complete |\n   597\t| first-1x100000gaps-uplot-vs-canvas | `20261118T023503Z-first-1x100000-gaps-uplot-vs-axylo-canvas-63ae` | complete |\n   598\t| first-1x100000gaps-uplot-vs-svg | `20261118T023535Z-first-1x100000-gaps-uplot-vs-axylo-svg-2505` | complete |\n   599\t| first-1x1000000-canvas-vs-svg | `20261118T023607Z-first-1x1000000-axylo-canvas-vs-axylo-svg-f230` | complete |\n   600\t| first-1x1000000-uplot-vs-canvas | `20261118T023633Z-first-1x1000000-uplot-vs-axylo-canvas-9f6a` | complete |\n   601\t| first-1x1000000-uplot-vs-svg | `20261118T023656Z-first-1x1000000-uplot-vs-axylo-svg-50d6` | complete |\n   602\t| page-canvas-vs-svg | `20261118T023718Z-page-3x120-x24-axylo-canvas-vs-axylo-svg-41e7` | complete |\n   603\t| page-uplot-vs-canvas | `20261118T023750Z-page-3x120-x24-uplot-vs-axylo-canvas-c286` | complete |\n   604\t| page-uplot-vs-svg | `20261118T023821Z-page-3x120-x24-uplot-vs-axylo-svg-2fe5` | complete |\n   605\t| stream-canvas-vs-svg | `20261118T023853Z-stream-w600-axylo-canvas-vs-axylo-svg-5dcc` | complete |\n   606\t| stream-uplot-vs-canvas | `20261118T024054Z-stream-w600-uplot-vs-axylo-canvas-fcdf` | complete |\n   607\t| stream-uplot-vs-svg | `20261118T024228Z-stream-w600-uplot-vs-axylo-svg-9b50` | complete |\n   608\t| theme-canvas-vs-svg | `20261118T024403Z-theme-3x120-axylo-canvas-vs-axylo-svg-b139` | complete |\n   609\t| theme-uplot-vs-canvas | `20261118T024504Z-theme-3x120-uplot-vs-axylo-canvas-0f67` | complete |\n   610\t| resize-1x100000-canvas-vs-svg | `20261118T024512Z-resize-1x100000-axylo-canvas-vs-axylo-svg-c11f` | complete |\n   611\t| resize-1x100000-uplot-vs-canvas | `20261118T024629Z-resize-1x100000-uplot-vs-axylo-canvas-0931` | complete |\n   612\t| resize-1x100000-uplot-vs-svg | `20261118T024729Z-resize-1x100000-uplot-vs-axylo-svg-a9cd` | complete |\n   613\t| resize-page-canvas-vs-svg | `20261118T024828Z-resize-3x120-x24-axylo-canvas-vs-axylo-svg-2888` | complete |\n   614\t| resize-page-uplot-vs-canvas | `20261118T024945Z-resize-3x120-x24-uplot-vs-axylo-canvas-d863` | complete |\n   615\t| resize-page-uplot-vs-svg | `20261118T025045Z-resize-3x120-x24-uplot-vs-axylo-svg-0221` | complete |\n   616\t| dpr2-first-1x100000-canvas-vs-svg | `20261118T025144Z-first-1x100000-dpr2-axylo-canvas-vs-axylo-svg-f780` | complete |\n   617\t| dpr2-first-1x100000-uplot-vs-canvas | `20261118T025210Z-first-1x100000-dpr2-uplot-vs-axylo-canvas-7d7a` | complete |\n   618\t| dpr2-first-1x100000-uplot-vs-svg | `20261118T025235Z-first-1x100000-dpr2-uplot-vs-axylo-svg-cb75` | complete |\n   619\t| dpr2-page-canvas-vs-svg | `20261118T025300Z-page-3x120-x24-dpr2-axylo-canvas-vs-axylo-svg-1121` | complete |\n   620\t| dpr2-page-uplot-vs-canvas | `20261118T025324Z-page-3x120-x24-dpr2-uplot-vs-axylo-canvas-29a0` | complete |\n   621\t| dpr2-page-uplot-vs-svg | `20261118T025349Z-page-3x120-x24-dpr2-uplot-vs-axylo-svg-2b25` | complete |\n   622\t\n   623\t## Limits\n   624\t\n   625\t- One browser (Chrome stable, headless) on one machine. No Firefox, Safari/WebKit, Edge, phone or throttled profile.\n   626\t- Headless Chrome here rasterizes WebGL with SwiftShader. No configuration measured here uses WebGL, but GPU raster of\n   627\t  Canvas 2D and SVG is not measured either: main-thread task time and process CPU times are what was recorded, and the\n   628\t  GPU process figures come from a headless browser whose raster path may differ from a headed browser with a GPU.\n   629\t- The machine was under load from other agents' tests during the whole session (load average above). The A-versus-A\n   630\t  bands are from the same session and show what that noise does to these workloads; they are one session, not three.\n   631\t- Process CPU times (`rendererCpuMs`, `gpuCpuMs`) come from `SystemInfo.getProcessInfo`, whose resolution here is\n   632\t  10 ms: useful for the 2 s resize window, too coarse for single charts.\n   633\t- Readiness comes from Axylo's benchmark hook (`chart.__bench.ready()`) and uPlot's draw hook; it is not validated\n   634\t  against screenshots. The admission check reads back ranges, counts and ends, not pixels (except in the theme\n   635\t  workload, which samples mark colors).\n   636\t- Theme: the per-toggle window is fixed (three animation frames plus 50 ms). Frames until the marks changed color\n   637\t  are measured in four separate untimed toggles. uPlot has no theme mechanism; its marks keep their colors, so it is\n   638\t  recorded as not admitted for this workload and not compared.\n   639\t- Memory figures are Linux process figures (PSS), not Chrome task-manager figures, and the canvas figure is calculated.\n   640\t- 1×1,000,000 used 4 blocks per comparison, fewer than the 8 used elsewhere; stream, resize and dpr 2 comparisons\n   641\t  against uPlot used 6.\n     1\t# Decision 0002: SVG paths draw the marks by default\n     2\t\n     3\tStatus: decided from the M1 measurements, by the coordinator, on 2026-11-18. The owner asked for this to be settled by measurement. It reverses the working assumption in the plan (Canvas 2D) and can be reversed again by one internal switch if the measurements still missing say otherwise.\n     4\t\n     5\tEvidence: [bench/results/m1-renderer-comparison.md](../../bench/results/m1-renderer-comparison.md). One session of 39 runs, production build, headless Chrome 157, machine under load from other work, A-versus-A noise bands for two workloads only.\n     6\t\n     7\t## What was measured\n     8\t\n     9\tCanvas → SVG, medians of main-thread task time unless stated. \"Lower\" means the 95% interval cleared zero and the noise band where one existed.\n    10\t\n    11\t| Workload | Canvas | SVG | Verdict |\n    12\t|---|---|---|---|\n    13\t| Streaming, per update | 2.26 ms | 1.45 ms | SVG lower |\n    14\t| Theme change, per toggle | 2.68 ms and 27 drawing calls | 2.01 ms and no drawing call | SVG lower |\n    15\t| Resize, one chart of 100,000 points | 915 ms | 472 ms | SVG lower on the main thread |\n    16\t| Same, CPU across all threads | 1,035 ms | 1,770 ms | **SVG higher** |\n    17\t| Resize, 24-chart page | 730 ms | 525 ms | SVG lower |\n    18\t| First chart, 10,000 points | 34.0 ms | 28.4 ms | SVG lower |\n    19\t| 24-chart page at pixel ratio 2 | 199 ms | 158 ms | SVG lower |\n    20\t| First chart, 3 × 120 | 23.6 ms | 19.8 ms | Inconclusive |\n    21\t| First chart, 100,000 points | 81.8 ms | 83.5 ms | Inconclusive |\n    22\t| First chart, 1,000,000 points | 622 ms | 652 ms | Inconclusive (4 blocks) |\n    23\t| Memory, 24-chart page at pixel ratio 2 | 34.2 MiB renderer, 11.5 MiB GPU, 7.7 MiB backing stores | 17.7 MiB, 2.2 MiB, none | SVG lower; its JavaScript heap is 0.1–0.3 MiB higher and it has 144 more DOM nodes |\n    24\t\n    25\tNo frame was later than 25 ms in any configuration, so frame pacing does not separate the two.\n    26\t\n    27\t## Why SVG\n    28\t\n    29\t1. Where the two differ on the main thread, SVG is ahead; where they do not differ, the measurements cannot tell them apart. Nothing measured favours canvas except CPU summed over all threads during a continuous resize of a 100,000-point chart.\n    30\t2. The drawing is simplified to a few vertices per pixel column before either renderer sees it, so a path's size is bounded by the plot width, not by the data. That removes the usual reason to prefer canvas for large series.\n    31\t3. SVG follows the page without code: a theme change restyles the marks with no call, forced colors and print work through CSS, browser zoom stays sharp, and there is no backing store to size, cap or lose.\n    32\t4. It uses roughly half the renderer memory on a dashboard page.\n    33\t\n    34\t## What this does not establish\n    35\t\n    36\t- **GPU rasterization was not measured.** Headless Chrome rasterizes in software here. The one result against SVG (all-thread CPU while resizing) is raster work; on a GPU it may shrink or grow.\n    37\t- **Dense point marks were not measured.** A scatter chart with tens of thousands of markers is the case most likely to favour canvas.\n    38\t- **One browser, one machine, one session.** Firefox and Safari may order the two differently.\n    39\t- Both renderers are far from uPlot (about 80 ms against 12 ms at 100,000 points). The profiles put that in data normalization and garbage collection, not in drawing (2–3%), so the renderer choice does not decide the performance budgets.\n    40\t\n    41\t## Consequences\n    42\t\n    43\t- The default mark renderer is SVG. The canvas renderer stays in the code behind the same internal switch, with the pixel-agreement tests between the two kept.\n    44\t- Before 1.0: measure scatter at 10,000, 50,000 and 200,000 points with both renderers and decide whether scatter above some size should use canvas automatically. If it never should, the canvas renderer is removed from the 1.0 bundle to save bytes.\n    45\t- When a real GPU and a second browser are available: rerun the resize and million-point workloads headed. If canvas wins there by more than the shipping thresholds in the performance plan, flip the switch back.\n    46\t- The plan's sections 2.2 and 2.3 are read with SVG in the \"marks\" position: a theme change no longer needs a redraw, and device pixel ratio matters only to simplification.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
