 page (same run). *Renderer PSS* and *GPU PSS* are the\n   257\tproportional set sizes of the page's renderer process and of the GPU process from Linux `/proc/<pid>/smaps_rollup`\n   258\t(CDP exposes no per-process memory; the page's renderer is the one that used the most CPU during the run), with the\n   259\tchart minus with only the data. *Canvas backing (calculated)* is width × height × 4 bytes over the chart canvases in\n   260\tdevice pixels; it is arithmetic, not a measurement, and the browser may hold more (double buffers, GPU copies).\n   261\tAll in MiB; medians of per-run values.\n   262\t\n   263\t### dpr 1, W-first 1×100,000\n   264\t\n   265\t| Comparison | Metric | Pairs/blocks | Median A | Median B | B − A [95% CI] | B/A − 1 | Outcome for B | Noise band |\n   266\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n   267\t| Canvas (A) vs SVG (B) | heapChartBytes (MiB) | 8/8 | 9.57 | 9.67 | 0.10 [0.10, 0.10] | +1.0% | **worse** | [-0.00, 0.00] |\n   268\t| Canvas (A) vs SVG (B) | rendererPssChartBytes (MiB) | 8/8 | 26.08 | 23.78 | -2.30 [-2.54, -2.03] | -8.8% | **better** | [-0.44, 0.50] |\n   269\t| Canvas (A) vs SVG (B) | gpuPssChartBytes (MiB) | 8/8 | 0.81 | 0.42 | -0.39 [-0.42, -0.35] | -48.3% | **better** | [-0.01, 0.03] |\n   270\t| Canvas (A) vs SVG (B) | canvasBackingBytes (MiB) | 8/8 | 1.15 | 0.00 | -1.15 [-1.15, -1.15] | -100.0% | **better** | [0.00, 0.00] |\n   271\t| Canvas (A) vs SVG (B) | domNodes (nodes) | 8/8 | 58.00 | 96.00 | 38.00 [38.00, 38.00] | +65.5% | **worse** | [0.00, 0.00] |\n   272\t| Canvas (A) vs SVG (B) | rendererPssBytes (MiB) | 8/8 | 81.77 | 79.54 | -2.23 [-2.44, -1.99] | -2.7% | **better** | [-0.39, 0.46] |\n   273\t| Canvas (A) vs SVG (B) | gpuPssBytes (MiB) | 8/8 | 39.19 | 38.77 | -0.42 [-0.53, -0.30] | -1.1% | **better** | [-0.24, 0.11] |\n   274\t| uPlot (A) vs Canvas (B) | heapChartBytes (MiB) | 8/8 | 0.25 | 9.57 | 9.31 [9.31, 9.32] | +3675.8% | **worse** | [-0.00, 0.00] |\n   555\t| `observe @ data/store-calendar.ts:1673` |