e-3x120-x24-dpr2-uplot-vs-axylo-canvas-29a0` | complete |\n   621\t| dpr2-page-uplot-vs-svg | `20261118T025349Z-page-3x120-x24-dpr2-uplot-vs-axylo-svg-2b25` | complete |\n   622\t\n   623\t## Limits\n   624\t\n   625\t- One browser (Chrome stable, headless) on one machine. No Firefox, Safari/WebKit, Edge, phone or throttled profile.\n   626\t- Headless Chrome here rasterizes WebGL with SwiftShader. No configuration measured here uses WebGL, but GPU raster of\n   627\t  Canvas 2D and SVG is not measured either: main-thread task time and process CPU times are what was recorded, and the\n   628\t  GPU process figures come from a headless browser whose raster path may differ from a headed browser with a GPU.\n   629\t- The machine was under load from other agents' tests during the whole session (load average above). The A-versus-A\n   630\t  bands are from the same session and show what that noise does to these workloads; they are one session, not three.\n   631\t- Process CPU times (`rendererCpuMs`, `gpuCpuMs`) come from `SystemInfo.getProcessInfo`, whose resolution here is\n   632\t  10 ms: useful for the 2 s resize window, too coarse for single charts.\n   633\t- Readiness comes from Axylo's benchmark hook (`chart.__bench.ready()`) and uPlot's draw hook; it is not validated\n   634\t  against screenshots. The admission check reads back ranges, counts and ends, not pixels (except in the theme\n   635\t  workload, which samples mark colors).\n   636\t- Theme: the per-toggle window is fixed (three animation frames plus 50 ms). Frames until the marks changed color\n   637\t  are measured in four separate untimed toggles. uPlot has no theme mechanism; its marks keep their colors, so it is\n   638\t  recorded as not admitted for this workload and not compared.\n   639\t- Memory figures are Linux process figures (PSS), not Chrome task-manager figures, and the canvas figure is calculated.\n   640\t- 1×1,000,000 used 4 blocks per comparison, fewer than the 8 used elsewhere; stream, resize and dpr 2 comparisons\n   641\t  against uPlot used 6.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba bench/results/make-m1-report.mjs; nl -ba bench/results/m1-session.sh; nl -ba bench/results/m1-runs.tsv'","aggregated_output":"     1\t#!/usr/bin/env node\n     2\t// Builds bench/results/m1-renderer-comparison.md from the history records listed in bench/results/m1-runs.tsv and\n     3\t// the profile summaries in bench/results/profiles. Numbers come only from those files.\n     4\t//   node bench/results/make-m1-report.mjs\n     5\timport fs from 'node:fs';\n     6\timport path from 'node:path';\n     7\timport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n     8\t\n     9\tconst HERE = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\n    10\tconst BENCH = path.resolve(HERE, '..');\n    11\tconst list = fs.readFileSync(path.join(HERE, 'm1-runs.tsv'), 'utf8').trim().split('\\n').map(l => l.split('\\t'));\n    12\tconst runs = Object.fromEntries(list.map(([label, id]) => {\n    13\t  const f = path.join(BENCH, 'history', `${id}.json`);\n    14\t  return [label, fs.existsSync(f) ? JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(f, 'utf8')) : null];\n    15\t}));\n    16\tconst ids = Object.fromEntries(list);\n    17\t\n    18\tconst num = (v, d = 2) => (typeof v !== 'number' || !Number.isFinite(v) ? 'n/a' : Math.abs(v) >= 1000 ? v.toFixed(0) : Math.abs(v) >= 100 ? v.toFixed(1) : v.toFixed(d));\n    19\tconst mib = v => (typeof v !== 'number' || !Number.isFinite(v) ? 'n/a' : `${(v / 2 ** 20).toFixed(2)}`);\n    20\tconst fmtFor = m => (m.unit === 'bytes' ? mib : v => num(v));\n    21\tconst pct = v => (v == null || !Number.isFinite(v) ? 'n/a' : `${v >= 0 ? '+' : ''}${(v * 100).toFixed(1)}%`);\n    22\tconst NAMES = { 'axylo-canvas': 'Canvas', 'axylo-svg': 'SVG', uplot: 'uPlot' };\n    23\t\n    24\tfunction row(label, metricKey) {\n    25\t  const r = runs[label];\n    26\t  if (!r) return `| ${label} | missing | | | | | | |`;\n    27\t  if (r.analysis?.notCompared) return `| ${NAMES[r.design.baseline]} (A) vs ${NAMES[r.design.candidate]} (B) | not compared: ${r.analysis.notCompared.join('; ').replace(/\\|/g, '\\\\|')} | | | | | | | |`;\n    28\t  const m = r.analysis?.metrics?.[metricKey];\n    29\t  if (!m) return `| ${NAMES[r.design.baseline]} → ${NAMES[r.design.candidate]} | ${metricKey}: not recorded | | | | | | |`;\n    30\t  if (m.na) return `| ${NAMES[r.design.baseline]} → ${NAMES[r.design.candidate]} | ${metricKey} | ${m.na} | | | | | |`;\n    31\t  const f = fmtFor(m);\n    32\t  const band = typeof m.noiseBand === 'object' ? `[${f(m.noiseBand.lo)}, ${f(m.noiseBand.hi)}]` : 'none';\n    33\t  return `| ${NAMES[r.design.baseline]} (A) vs ${NAMES[r.design.candidate]} (B) | ${metricKey}${m.unit === 'bytes' ? ' (MiB)' : m.unit === 'ms' ? ' (ms)' : ` (${m.unit})`} | ${m.pairs}/${r.design.blocks} | ${f(m.medianA)} | ${f(m.medianB)} | ${f(m.diff)} [${f(m.lo)}, ${f(m.hi)}] | ${pct(m.relative)} | **${m.outcome}**${m.outcomeNote ? ' (few pairs)' : ''} | ${band} |`;\n    34\t}\n    35\tconst HEAD = '| Comparison | Metric | Pairs/blocks | Median A | Median B | B − A [95% CI] | B/A − 1 | Outcome for B | Noise band |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|';\n    36\tconst table = (labels, metrics) => [HEAD, ...labels.flatMap(l => (runs[l]?.analysis?.notCompared ? [row(l, metrics[0])] : metrics.map(k => row(l, k))))].join('\\n');\n    37\t\n    38\tconst out = [];\n    39\tconst first = Object.values(runs).find(Boolean);\n    40\tconst env = first.environment;\n    41\tconst allRuns = Object.values(runs).filter(Boolean);\n    42\tconst loads = allRuns.flatMap(r => [r.environment.loadAverageAtStart?.[0], r.environment.loadAverageAtEnd?.[0]]).filter(Number.isFinite);\n    43\tconst pageEnv = env.page ?? {};\n    44\tconst starts = allRuns.map(r => r.startedAt).sort(), ends = allRuns.map(r => r.finishedAt).filter(Boolean).sort();\n    45\t\n    46\tout.push(`# M1 renderer comparison: Axylo Canvas 2D against SVG\n    47\t\n    48\tGenerated by \\`bench/results/make-m1-report.mjs\\` from the history records listed in \\`bench/results/m1-runs.tsv\\`\n    49\t(session script \\`bench/results/m1-session.sh\\`). Observations only; this file does not recommend a renderer.\n    50\t\n    51\tHow to read the tables: every comparison runs A and B in randomized balanced blocks (as many AB as BA), a fresh\n    52\tbrowser context per run. \"Median A / B\" are medians of per-run values; \"B − A\" is the difference of medians with a\n    53\tpaired bootstrap 95% interval over blocks. **Outcome is for B relative to A, and lower is better for every metric**:\n    54\tin \"Canvas (A) vs SVG (B)\", *better* means SVG measured lower, *worse* means SVG measured higher. *Inconclusive*\n    55\tmeans the interval includes zero (or the noise band); it never means \"no difference\". Where a noise band is shown,\n    56\tthe interval had to clear it as well as zero; the band is the union of the two A-versus-A intervals (Canvas and SVG)\n    57\tfor that workload, from this session. Workloads without an A-versus-A band are classified against zero only.\n    58\tMethod and metric definitions: \\`bench/README.md\\`.\n    59\t\n    60\t## Environment\n    61\t\n    62\t| | |\n    63\t|---|---|\n    64\t| Session | ${starts[0]} to ${ends[ends.length - 1]} (UTC) |\n    65\t| Browser | ${env.browser.name} ${env.browser.version}, ${env.browser.headless ? 'headless' : 'headed'}; Playwright ${env.playwright}; Node ${env.node} |\n    66\t| Machine | ${env.cpu.model}, ${env.cpu.logicalCores} logical cores, governor ${env.cpu.governor}, ${env.memoryGiB} GiB; ${env.os.name} (${env.os.type} ${env.os.release}) |\n    67\t| Load | 1-minute load average between ${Math.min(...loads).toFixed(1)} and ${Math.max(...loads).toFixed(1)} at run starts and ends; other agents were running tests on the machine |\n    68\t| Display | ${pageEnv.refresh ? `${pageEnv.refresh.hz} Hz observed by the page` : 'n/a'}; viewport 1,440×900; device pixel ratio 1 unless marked dpr 2 |\n    69\t| WebGL renderer | ${pageEnv.webglRenderer ?? 'n/a'} (software; not used by any configuration measured here) |\n    70\t| Axylo | production build \\`axylo.iife.min.js\\` sha256 ${env.axyloBundles?.['axylo.iife.min.js']?.sha256?.slice(0, 16)}…, with \\`__AXYLO_BENCH__\\` set; development build \\`axylo.iife.js\\` sha256 ${env.axyloBundles?.['axylo.iife.js']?.sha256?.slice(0, 16)}… (profiles only). Both are the snapshot of \\`packages/axylo/dist\\` taken once at the start of the session (built ${JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(BENCH, 'dist/manifest.json'), 'utf8')).axylo?.['axylo.iife.min.js']?.builtAt ?? 'n/a'}). Library sources had uncommitted changes at the time: ${String(env.axyloBundles?.gitStatusOfLibrarySources ?? 'n/a').replace(/\\n/g, ', ')} |\n    71\t| Commit | ${env.commit} |\n    72\t| Libraries | uPlot ${env.libraries.uplot}; Axylo ${env.libraries.axylo} |\n    73\t`);\n    74\t\n    75\t// Summary of every Canvas-vs-SVG metric, generated from the same records as the tables below.\n    76\t{\n    77\t  const cmp = [\n    78\t    ['W-first 3×120', 'first-3x120-canvas-vs-svg'], ['W-first 1×10,000', 'first-1x10000-canvas-vs-svg'],\n    79\t    ['W-first 1×100,000', 'first-1x100000-canvas-vs-svg'], ['W-first 1×100,000 gaps', 'first-1x100000gaps-canvas-vs-svg'],\n    80\t    ['W-first 1×1,000,000', 'first-1x1000000-canvas-vs-svg'], ['W-page', 'page-canvas-vs-svg'], ['W-stream', 'stream-canvas-vs-svg'],\n    81\t    ['Theme', 'theme-canvas-vs-svg'], ['Resize 1×100,000', 'resize-1x100000-canvas-vs-svg'], ['Resize 24 charts', 'resize-page-canvas-vs-svg'],\n    82\t    ['W-first 1×100,000 dpr 2', 'dpr2-first-1x100000-canvas-vs-svg'], ['W-page dpr 2', 'dpr2-page-canvas-vs-svg'],\n    83\t  ];\n    84\t  out.push(`## Canvas against SVG: every metric with a verdict\n    85\t\n    86\tGenerated list of the Canvas (A) vs SVG (B) comparisons. \"SVG lower\" = outcome *better* for SVG, \"SVG higher\" =\n    87\t*worse*. Metrics whose outcome was inconclusive are counted, not listed; the full tables follow.\n    88\t\n    89\t| Workload | SVG lower (better) | SVG higher (worse) | Inconclusive |\n    90\t|---|---|---|---|`);\n    91\t  for (const [name, label] of cmp) {\n    92\t    const ms = Object.entries(runs[label]?.analysis?.metrics ?? {});\n    93\t    const f = (m, k) => `${k} ${fmtFor(m)(m.medianA)} → ${fmtFor(m)(m.medianB)}${m.unit === 'bytes' ? ' MiB' : m.unit === 'ms' ? ' ms' : ''}`;\n    94\t    const lower = ms.filter(([, m]) => m.outcome === 'better').map(([k, m]) => f(m, k));\n    95\t    const higher = ms.filter(([, m]) => m.outcome === 'worse').map(([k, m]) => f(m, k));\n    96\t    const inc = ms.filter(([, m]) => m.outcome === 'inconclusive').length;\n    97\t    out.push(`| ${name} | ${lower.join('; ') || '–'} | ${higher.join('; ') || '–'} | ${inc}${ms.some(([, m]) => m.outcomeNote) ? ' (fewer than 6 pairs: all inconclusive by rule)' : ''} |`);\n    98\t  }\n    99\t  out.push(`\n   100\tReading notes: frame timestamps are quantized to 0.1 ms, so frame-interval differences of 0.1 ms or less are\n   101\tquantization, even where the rule calls them better or worse; process CPU times have a 10 ms resolution. The\n   102\tA-versus-A bands for \\`taskMs\\` are wide because a few runs in those sessions were much slower than the rest (the\n   103\tmachine was loaded); the comparisons on those workloads had to clear them.\n   104\t`);\n   105\t}\n   106\t\n   107\t// Noise\n   108\tout.push(`## Noise bands (A versus A, same session)\n   109\t\n   110\t| Run | Workload | Metric | Pairs | Median A | Median A' | A' − A [95% CI] |\n   111\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|`);\n   112\tfor (const label of ['aa-canvas-first-100k', 'aa-svg-first-100k', 'aa-canvas-page', 'aa-svg-page']) {\n   113\t  const r = runs[label];\n   114\t  if (!r?.analysis?.metrics) { out.push(`| ${label} | missing | | | | | |`); continue; }\n   115\t  for (const k of ['taskMs', 'readyFrameMs', 'heapChartBytes', 'rendererPssChartBytes']) {\n   116\t    const m = r.analysis.metrics[k];\n   117\t    if (!m || m.na) continue;\n   118\t    const f = fmtFor(m);\n   119\t    out.push(`| ${NAMES[r.design.baseline]} | ${r.design.workload} ${r.design.params.size}${r.design.workload === 'page' ? ' ×24' : ''} | ${k}${m.unit === 'bytes' ? ' (MiB)' : ' (ms)'} | ${m.pairs} | ${f(m.medianA)} | ${f(m.medianB)} | ${f(m.diff)} [${f(m.lo)}, ${f(m.hi)}] |`);\n   120\t  }\n   121\t}\n   122\tout.push('\\nOne session only (the plan asks for bands from at least three sessions).\\n');\n   123\t\n   124\tconst sections = [\n   125\t  ['W-first, 3×120', ['first-3x120-canvas-vs-svg', 'first-3x120-uplot-vs-canvas', 'first-3x120-uplot-vs-svg'], ['taskMs', 'readyFrameMs', 'scriptMs', 'layoutStyleMs']],\n   126\t  ['W-first, 1×10,000', ['first-1x10000-canvas-vs-svg', 'first-1x10000-uplot-vs-canvas', 'first-1x10000-uplot-vs-svg'], ['taskMs', 'readyFrameMs', 'scriptMs', 'layoutStyleMs']],\n   127\t  ['W-first, 1×100,000', ['first-1x100000-canvas-vs-svg', 'first-1x100000-uplot-vs-canvas', 'first-1x100000-uplot-vs-svg'], ['taskMs', 'readyFrameMs', 'scriptMs', 'layoutStyleMs']],\n   128\t  ['W-first, 1×100,000 with 5% missing in runs', ['first-1x100000gaps-canvas-vs-svg', 'first-1x100000gaps-uplot-vs-canvas', 'first-1x100000gaps-uplot-vs-svg'], ['taskMs', 'readyFrameMs']],\n   129\t  ['W-first, 1×1,000,000 (4 blocks)', ['first-1x1000000-canvas-vs-svg', 'first-1x1000000-uplot-vs-canvas', 'first-1x1000000-uplot-vs-svg'], ['taskMs', 'readyFrameMs']],\n   130\t  ['W-page, 24 charts of 3×120', ['page-canvas-vs-svg', 'page-uplot-vs-canvas', 'page-uplot-vs-svg'], ['taskMs', 'readyFrameMs', 'scriptMs', 'layoutStyleMs']],\n   131\t  ['W-stream, 600-point window, 300 samples at 60 Hz from an independent clock', ['stream-canvas-vs-svg', 'stream-uplot-vs-canvas', 'stream-uplot-vs-svg'], ['taskMsPerUpdate', 'delayP95Ms', 'maxBacklog', 'framesOverThreshold', 'frameP99Ms', 'createTaskMs']],\n   132\t  ['Theme toggle, 3×120, 20 toggles', ['theme-canvas-vs-svg', 'theme-uplot-vs-canvas'], ['taskMsPerToggle', 'taskMsToggleMax', 'canvasCallsPerToggle', 'mutationsPerToggle', 'framesToNewColor']],\n   133\t  ['Resize 1,200 → 400 → 1,200 px over 2 s, one chart of 1×100,000', ['resize-1x100000-canvas-vs-svg', 'resize-1x100000-uplot-vs-canvas', 'resize-1x100000-uplot-vs-svg'], ['taskMs', 'frameP95Ms', 'frameP99Ms', 'framesOverThreshold', 'frameMaxMs', 'rendererCpuMs', 'gpuCpuMs']],\n   134\t  ['Resize, 24-chart page', ['resize-page-canvas-vs-svg', 'resize-page-uplot-vs-canvas', 'resize-page-uplot-vs-svg'], ['taskMs', 'frameP95Ms', 'frameP99Ms', 'framesOverThreshold', 'frameMaxMs', 'rendererCpuMs', 'gpuCpuMs']],\n   135\t];\n   136\tfor (const [title, labels, metrics] of sections) {\n   137\t  out.push(`## ${title}\\n\\n${table(labels, metrics)}\\n`);\n   138\t  const bad = labels.flatMap(l => (runs[l]?.runs ?? []).filter(x => x.phase === 'timed' && x.outcome !== 'ok').map(x => `${l} block ${x.block} ${x.ref ?? x.adapter}: ${x.outcome}${x.reason ? ` (${String(x.reason).slice(0, 160)})` : ''}`));\n   139\t  if (bad.length) out.push(`Runs not paired: ${bad.join('; ')}\\n`);\n   140\t}\n   141\t\n   142\tout.push(`## Memory\n   143\t\n   144\tFour figures, never added together. *JS heap* is \\`Runtime.getHeapUsage\\` used size after \\`HeapProfiler.collectGarbage\\`,\n   145\twith the chart minus with only the input data on the page (same run). *Renderer PSS* and *GPU PSS* are the\n   146\tproportional set sizes of the page's renderer process and of the GPU process from Linux \\`/proc/<pid>/smaps_rollup\\`\n   147\t(CDP exposes no per-process memory; the page's renderer is the one that used the most CPU during the run), with the\n   148\tchart minus with only the data. *Canvas backing (calculated)* is width × height × 4 bytes over the chart canvases in\n   149\tdevice pixels; it is arithmetic, not a measurement, and the browser may hold more (double buffers, GPU copies).\n   150\tAll in MiB; medians of per-run values.\n   151\t`);\n   152\tfor (const [title, labels] of [\n   153\t  ['dpr 1, W-first 1×100,000', ['first-1x100000-canvas-vs-svg', 'first-1x100000-uplot-vs-canvas', 'first-1x100000-uplot-vs-svg']],\n   154\t  ['dpr 2, W-first 1×100,000', ['dpr2-first-1x100000-canvas-vs-svg', 'dpr2-first-1x100000-uplot-vs-canvas', 'dpr2-first-1x100000-uplot-vs-svg']],\n   155\t  ['dpr 1, W-first 3×120', ['first-3x120-canvas-vs-svg', 'first-3x120-uplot-vs-canvas', 'first-3x120-uplot-vs-svg']],\n   156\t  ['dpr 1, W-page (24 charts)', ['page-canvas-vs-svg', 'page-uplot-vs-canvas', 'page-uplot-vs-svg']],\n   157\t  ['dpr 2, W-page (24 charts)', ['dpr2-page-canvas-vs-svg', 'dpr2-page-uplot-vs-canvas', 'dpr2-page-uplot-vs-svg']],\n   158\t]) out.push(`### ${title}\\n\\n${table(labels, ['heapChartBytes', 'rendererPssChartBytes', 'gpuPssChartBytes', 'canvasBackingBytes', 'domNodes', 'rendererPssBytes', 'gpuPssBytes'])}\\n`);\n   159\tout.push(`Timing at dpr 2 (same runs):\\n\\n${table(['dpr2-first-1x100000-canvas-vs-svg', 'dpr2-first-1x100000-uplot-vs-canvas', 'dpr2-first-1x100000-uplot-vs-svg', 'dpr2-page-canvas-vs-svg', 'dpr2-page-uplot-vs-canvas', 'dpr2-page-uplot-vs-svg'], ['taskMs'])}\\n`);\n   160\t\n   161\t// Profiles\n   162\tconst profDir = path.join(HERE, 'profiles');\n   163\tconst profs = fs.existsSync(profDir) ? fs.readdirSync(profDir).filter(f => f.endsWith('.summary.json')).sort().map(f => JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(profDir, f), 'utf8'))) : [];\n   164\tout.push(`## CPU profiles\n   165\t\n   166\tOne Chrome CPU profile per renderer and build (CDP \\`Profiler\\`, 100 µs sampling), from the create call to the end of\n   167\tthe 500 ms settle window, at the two sizes where the uPlot gap was examined (3×120 and 1×100,000). Profiled runs\n   168\tare slowed by the profiler and are not timings. Each sample is attributed to the deepest Axylo frame on its stack,\n   169\tand that frame's source module gives the stage (\\`bench/lib/profile-summary.mjs\\`: data/ → normalize; view/, scale/\n   170\t→ view; layout/, format/ → layout; scene/, simplify/ → scene; render/ → draw; dom/ → DOM; core/ etc. → orchestration).\n   171\tPercentages are of busy time (all samples except idle). Raw \\`.cpuprofile\\` files are next to the summaries in\n   172\t\\`bench/results/profiles/\\` and open in Chrome DevTools.\n   173\t`);\n   174\tfor (const size of ['3x120', '1x100000']) {\n   175\t  for (const renderer of ['canvas', 'svg']) {\n   176\t    for (const build of ['dev', 'prod']) {\n   177\t      const p = profs.find(x => x.params.size === size && x.adapter === `axylo:renderer=${renderer},build=${build}`);\n   178\t      if (!p) { out.push(`**${size}, ${renderer}, ${build}**: profile missing.\\n`); continue; }\n   179\t      const s = p.summary;\n   180\t      out.push(`**${size}, ${renderer}, ${build === 'dev' ? 'development build' : 'production build'}** — busy ${num(s.busyMs)} ms (${s.samples} samples); mapping: ${s.mapping}. File \\`${p.profileFile}\\`.\\n`);\n   181\t      out.push('| Stage | ms | % of busy |\\n|---|---|---|');\n   182\t      for (const st of s.stages.filter(x => x.k !== '(idle)')) out.push(`| ${st.k} | ${num(st.ms)} | ${st.ofBusy}% |`);\n   183\t      if (build === 'dev') {\n   184\t        out.push('\\nTop functions (deepest Axylo frame; the line is in the bundle `axylo.iife.js`, not the source file):\\n\\n| Function @ module:bundle line | ms | % of busy |\\n|---|---|---|');\n   185\t        for (const fn of s.functions.slice(0, 8)) out.push(`| \\`${fn.k}\\` | ${num(fn.ms)} | ${fn.ofBusy}% |`);\n   186\t      }\n   187\t      out.push('');\n   188\t    }\n   189\t  }\n   190\t}\n   191\tout.push(`The development build runs \\`__DEV__\\` checks the production build does not, so its stage shares are a guide to\n   192\twhere time goes, not the production split. The production profiles could not be mapped to modules (see \"mapping\"),\n   193\tso for them only Axylo's total against garbage collection and native work is shown.\n   194\t`);\n   195\t\n   196\tout.push(`## Run ids\n   197\t\n   198\tAll in \\`bench/history/<run id>.json\\` (raw per-run samples, environment record, admission readback).\n   199\t\n   200\t| Label | Run id | Status |\n   201\t|---|---|---|\n   202\t${list.map(([l, id]) => `| ${l} | \\`${id}\\` | ${runs[l]?.status ?? 'missing'} |`).join('\\n')}\n   203\t\n   204\t## Limits\n   205\t\n   206\t- One browser (Chrome stable, headless) on one machine. No Firefox, Safari/WebKit, Edge, phone or throttled profile.\n   207\t- Headless Chrome here rasterizes WebGL with SwiftShader. No configuration measured here uses WebGL, but GPU raster of\n   208\t  Canvas 2D and SVG is not measured either: main-thread task time and process CPU times are what was recorded, and the\n   209\t  GPU process figures come from a headless browser whose raster path may differ from a headed browser with a GPU.\n   210\t- The machine was under load from other agents' tests during the whole session (load average above). The A-versus-A\n   211\t  bands are from the same session and show what that noise does to these workloads; they are one session, not three.\n   212\t- Process CPU times (\\`rendererCpuMs\\`, \\`gpuCpuMs\\`) come from \\`SystemInfo.getProcessInfo\\`, whose resolution here is\n   213\t  10 ms: useful for the 2 s resize window, too coarse for single charts.\n   214\t- Readiness comes from Axylo's benchmark hook (\\`chart.__bench.ready()\\`) and uPlot's draw hook; it is not validated\n   215\t  against screenshots. The admission check reads back ranges, counts and ends, not pixels (except in the theme\n   216\t  workload, which samples mark colors).\n   217\t- Theme: the per-toggle window is fixed (three animation frames plus 50 ms). Frames until the marks changed color\n   218\t  are measured in four separate untimed toggles. uPlot has no theme mechanism; its marks keep their colors, so it is\n   219\t  recorded as not admitted for this workload and not compared.\n   220\t- Memory figures are Linux process figures (PSS), not Chrome task-manager figures, and the canvas figure is calculated.\n   221\t- 1×1,000,000 used 4 blocks per comparison, fewer than the 8 used elsewhere; stream, resize and dpr 2 comparisons\n   222\t  against uPlot used 6.\n   223\t`);\n   224\t\n   225\tfs.writeFileSync(path.join(HERE, 'm1-renderer-comparison.md'), out.join('\\n'));\n   226\tconsole.log(`wrote bench/results/m1-renderer-comparison.md from ${allRuns.length} records and ${profs.length} profiles`);\n     1\t#!/bin/bash\n     2\t# M1 renderer comparison session: Axylo canvas against Axylo SVG, each against uPlot for reference.\n     3\t# One build (snapshot of packages/axylo/dist) at the start; every run after it uses --no-build so all runs measure the\n     4\t# same bytes. Runs are sequential. Run ids are appended to bench/results/m1-runs.tsv (label, run id).\n     5\tset -u\n     6\tcd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/../..\"\n     7\tLIST=bench/results/m1-runs.tsv\n     8\tLOG=bench/results/m1-session.log\n     9\t: > \"$LIST\"; : > \"$LOG\"\n    10\tnode bench/build.mjs | tee -a \"$LOG\"\n    11\trun() {\n    12\t  local label=$1; shift\n    13\t  local out; out=$(node bench/run.mjs --no-build \"$@\" 2>&1)\n    14\t  echo \"$out\" >> \"$LOG\"\n    15\t  local id; id=$(echo \"$out\" | awk '/^run /{print $2; exit}')\n    16\t  printf '%s\\t%s\\n' \"$label\" \"${id:-FAILED}\" >> \"$LIST\"\n    17\t  echo \"$(date +%T) $label -> ${id:-FAILED}\"\n    18\t}\n    19\tidof() { awk -F'\\t' -v l=\"$1\" '$1==l{print $2}' \"$LIST\"; }\n    20\t\n    21\t# Noise bands first, so the comparisons can be classified against them.\n    22\trun aa-canvas-first-100k --aa axylo-canvas --workload first --size 1x100000 --blocks 8\n    23\trun aa-svg-first-100k    --aa axylo-svg    --workload first --size 1x100000 --blocks 8\n    24\trun aa-canvas-page       --aa axylo-canvas --workload page --blocks 8\n    25\trun aa-svg-page          --aa axylo-svg    --workload page --blocks 8\n    26\tN100K=\"$(idof aa-canvas-first-100k),$(idof aa-svg-first-100k)\"\n    27\tNPAGE=\"$(idof aa-canvas-page),$(idof aa-svg-page)\"\n    28\t\n    29\tfor size in 3x120 1x10000 1x100000; do\n    30\t  noise=(); [ \"$size\" = 1x100000 ] && noise=(--noise \"$N100K\")\n    31\t  run \"first-$size-canvas-vs-svg\"   --baseline axylo-canvas --candidate axylo-svg    --workload first --size $size --blocks 8 \"${noise[@]}\"\n    32\t  run \"first-$size-uplot-vs-canvas\" --baseline uplot        --candidate axylo-canvas --workload first --size $size --blocks 8 \"${noise[@]}\"\n    33\t  run \"first-$size-uplot-vs-svg\"    --baseline uplot        --candidate axylo-svg    --workload first --size $size --blocks 8 \"${noise[@]}\"\n    34\tdone\n    35\trun first-1x100000gaps-canvas-vs-svg   --baseline axylo-canvas --candidate axylo-svg    --workload first --size 1x100000 --gaps --blocks 8\n    36\trun first-1x100000gaps-uplot-vs-canvas --baseline uplot        --candidate axylo-canvas --workload first --size 1x100000 --gaps --blocks 8\n    37\trun first-1x100000gaps-uplot-vs-svg    --baseline uplot        --candidate axylo-svg    --workload first --size 1x100000 --gaps --blocks 8\n    38\trun first-1x1000000-canvas-vs-svg   --baseline axylo-canvas --candidate axylo-svg    --workload first --size 1x1000000 --blocks 4\n    39\trun first-1x1000000-uplot-vs-canvas --baseline uplot        --candidate axylo-canvas --workload first --size 1x1000000 --blocks 4\n    40\trun first-1x1000000-uplot-vs-svg    --baseline uplot        --candidate axylo-svg    --workload first --size 1x1000000 --blocks 4\n    41\t\n    42\trun page-canvas-vs-svg   --baseline axylo-canvas --candidate axylo-svg    --workload page --blocks 8 --noise \"$NPAGE\"\n    43\trun page-uplot-vs-canvas --baseline uplot        --candidate axylo-canvas --workload page --blocks 8 --noise \"$NPAGE\"\n    44\trun page-uplot-vs-svg    --baseline uplot        --candidate axylo-svg    --workload page --blocks 8 --noise \"$NPAGE\"\n    45\t\n    46\trun stream-canvas-vs-svg   --baseline axylo-canvas --candidate axylo-svg    --workload stream --blocks 8\n    47\trun stream-uplot-vs-canvas --baseline uplot        --candidate axylo-canvas --workload stream --blocks 6\n    48\trun stream-uplot-vs-svg    --baseline uplot        --candidate axylo-svg    --workload stream --blocks 6\n    49\t\n    50\trun theme-canvas-vs-svg   --baseline axylo-canvas --candidate axylo-svg    --workload theme --blocks 8\n    51\trun theme-uplot-vs-canvas --baseline uplot        --candidate axylo-canvas --workload theme --blocks 2\n    52\t\n    53\trun resize-1x100000-canvas-vs-svg   --baseline axylo-canvas --candidate axylo-svg    --workload resize --size 1x100000 --blocks 8\n    54\trun resize-1x100000-uplot-vs-canvas --baseline uplot        --candidate axylo-canvas --workload resize --size 1x100000 --blocks 6\n    55\trun resize-1x100000-uplot-vs-svg    --baseline uplot        --candidate axylo-svg    --workload resize --size 1x100000 --blocks 6\n    56\trun resize-page-canvas-vs-svg   --baseline axylo-canvas --candidate axylo-svg    --workload resize --size 3x120 --charts 24 --blocks 8\n    57\trun resize-page-uplot-vs-canvas --baseline uplot        --candidate axylo-canvas --workload resize --size 3x120 --charts 24 --blocks 6\n    58\trun resize-page-uplot-vs-svg    --baseline uplot        --candidate axylo-svg    --workload resize --size 3x120 --charts 24 --blocks 6\n    59\t\n    60\t# Memory at device pixel ratio 2 (ratio 1 comes from the first/page runs above).\n    61\trun dpr2-first-1x100000-canvas-vs-svg   --baseline axylo-canvas --candidate axylo-svg    --workload first --size 1x100000 --dpr 2 --blocks 6\n    62\trun dpr2-first-1x100000-uplot-vs-canvas --baseline uplot        --candidate axylo-canvas --workload first --size 1x100000 --dpr 2 --blocks 6\n    63\trun dpr2-first-1x100000-uplot-vs-svg    --baseline uplot        --candidate axylo-svg    --workload first --size 1x100000 --dpr 2 --blocks 6\n    64\trun dpr2-page-canvas-vs-svg   --baseline axylo-canvas --candidate axylo-svg    --workload page --dpr 2 --blocks 6\n    65\trun dpr2-page-uplot-vs-canvas --baseline uplot        --candidate axylo-canvas --workload page --dpr 2 --blocks 6\n    66\trun dpr2-page-uplot-vs-svg    --baseline uplot        --candidate axylo-svg    --workload page --dpr 2 --blocks 6\n    67\t\n    68\t# CPU profiles (not timings): production and development builds of each renderer, at 3x120 and 1x100000.\n    69\tfor size in 3x120 1x100000; do\n    70\t  for r in canvas svg; do\n    71\t    for b in prod dev; do\n    72\t      node bench/profile.mjs --no-build --adapter \"axylo:renderer=$r,build=$b\" --size $size >> \"$LOG\" 2>&1 && echo \"$(date +%T) profile $size $r $b\"\n    73\t    done\n    74\t  done\n    75\tdone\n    76\techo SESSION-DONE | tee -a \"$LOG\"\n     1\taa-canvas-first-100k\t20261118T022750Z-first-1x100000-aa-axylo-canvas-4161\n     2\taa-svg-first-100k\t20261118T022821Z-first-1x100000-aa-axylo-svg-54f2\n     3\taa-canvas-page\t20261118T022851Z-page-3x120-x24-aa-axylo-canvas-567b\n     4\taa-svg-page\t20261118T022921Z-page-3x120-x24-aa-axylo-svg-ef71\n     5\tfirst-3x120-canvas-vs-svg\t20261118T022951Z-first-3x120-axylo-canvas-vs-axylo-svg-e741\n     6\tfirst-3x120-uplot-vs-canvas\t20261118T023022Z-first-3x120-uplot-vs-axylo-canvas-e472\n     7\tfirst-3x120-uplot-vs-svg\t20261118T023053Z-first-3x120-uplot-vs-axylo-svg-7ee1\n     8\tfirst-1x10000-canvas-vs-svg\t20261118T023123Z-first-1x10000-axylo-canvas-vs-axylo-svg-5eaa\n     9\tfirst-1x10000-uplot-vs-canvas\t20261118T023155Z-first-1x10000-uplot-vs-axylo-canvas-f92c\n    10\tfirst-1x10000-uplot-vs-svg\t20261118T023225Z-first-1x10000-uplot-vs-axylo-svg-a264\n    11\tfirst-1x100000-canvas-vs-svg\t20261118T023256Z-first-1x100000-axylo-canvas-vs-axylo-svg-7ca9\n    12\tfirst-1x100000-uplot-vs-canvas\t20261118T023328Z-first-1x100000-uplot-vs-axylo-canvas-6583\n    13\tfirst-1x100000-uplot-vs-svg\t20261118T023400Z-first-1x100000-uplot-vs-axylo-svg-