40 px; scene snapshot; resize in both directions with no call from the page.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:278:- 1,000 create–destroy cycles show no heap growth trend and no remaining listeners or observers.\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:95:| F2 | Missing values are never drawn as zero and never bridged unless the author asks. An explicit `null` is a gap, silently. An isolated value between two gaps is a visible point. A missing bar shows a \"no data\" mark at the baseline, distinct from a zero bar. On a time or date axis with a regular step, an absent step is a gap and raises AX105; `missing: 'zero'` on the field turns absent and null values into zeros for counts. Tooltip, table and announcements say \"No data\". | `trend` with nulls and `trend` with the same 7 rows deleted render the same gap; `dirty` fixtures; property test that no segment connects across a missing index | R5 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:104:| F11 | Line, area and scatter are drawn in x order whatever the input order. On line, area and bar, two rows with the same x in one series are AX108 and that series is not drawn. On scatter, points sharing an x (or both coordinates) are ordinary data. | Shuffled `trend` renders identically; duplicate fixture | R5 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:115:| L5 | A marker on every point appears only when adjacent points are at least 12 px apart (provisional value), and always for isolated points. | `trend` at 720 px has none; a 12-point line has them | R8 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:116:| L6 | Title, subtitle and axis titles with units are part of the chart. A value axis is titled with its label (the field name when none is given) and unit. An x axis that is a measure (number) is titled the same way; a time, date or category x axis is titled only when the author gives a `label`, since its ticks already say what it is. A reference line or band shows its label next to it. Axis titles never overlap tick labels. | Layout tests; `trend` fixture | R9 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:226:| DX5 | Three methods change a chart: `update` changes options, `append` adds rows, `zoom` sets the view. They apply in call order. Validation and diagnostics are synchronous; drawing is deferred to the next frame; marks, labels, hit testing and the accessibility layer always switch to a new state together. `destroy()` releases everything and cancels pending work. No `resize()` exists. | Sequence tests: replace then append then zoom in one turn; a rejected `strict` update leaves the last valid chart; destroy before the frame; 1,000 create–destroy cycles show no heap growth trend (P7) | D3, R16 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:241:| P1 | `trend` (3×120), default options, reference desktop | Main-thread task time from the call until the chart is complete | Median of 20 runs | 10 ms | Not comparable across libraries below about 35 ms with the Phase 1 method |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:245:| P5 | 24 `trend` charts created on one page | Total main-thread task time | Median of 20 | 200 ms | Not measured in Phase 1 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:248:| P7 | Memory | Bytes owned by Axylo beyond the caller's columns for 1,000,000 points; heap trend over 1,000 create–destroy cycles | Measured after forced collection | At most 1× the size of the caller's two columns; no upward slope | Not measured in Phase 1 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:297:| Which keyboard and screen-reader pattern for the plot? | Decide from the M1 spike: three candidate patterns on the `trend` chart, rehearsed on the five pairs. | M1 record, confirmed in M4. |\n./research/harness/shots/trend-highcharts.png\n./research/harness/shots/trend-highcharts-plain.png\n./research/harness/shots/trend-echarts-aria.png\n./research/harness/shots/trend-nivo.png\n./research/harness/shots/trend-d3.png\n./research/harness/shots/trend-apexcharts.png\n./research/harness/shots/trend-chartjs.png\n./research/harness/shots/trend-uplot.png\n./research/harness/shots/_sheet-trend.png\n./research/harness/shots/trend-recharts.png\n./research/harness/shots/trend-plotly.png\n./research/harness/shots/trend-mui.png\n./research/harness/shots/trend-echarts.png\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
