rue;\n   105\t  const summary = make('p', `axylo-summary ${HIDDEN}`);\n   106\t  summary.id = `${id}-s`;\n   107\t  const plot = make('div', 'axylo-plot');\n   108\t  const message = make('p', 'axylo-message');\n   109\t  message.id = `${id}-m`;\n   110\t  message.hidden = true;\n   111\t  const corner = make('span', 'axylo-corner');\n   112\t  corner.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');\n   113\t  corner.textContent = '*';\n   114\t  corner.hidden = true;\n   115\t  plot.append(parts.marks, parts.text, message, corner);\n   116\t  const note = make('p', 'axylo-note');\n   117\t  note.id = `${id}-n`;\n   118\t  note.setAttribute('role', 'status');\n   119\t  // A status that is not live: the note can change as streamed data arrives (labels thinned, values left\n   120\t  // out), and data arriving must not speak (spec A7). The summary carries the same statements.\n   121\t  note.setAttribute('aria-live', 'off');\n   122\t  note.hidden = true;\n   123\t  const live = make('div', `axylo-live ${HIDDEN}`);\n   124\t  live.setAttribute('aria-live', 'polite');\n   125\t  const tooltip = make('div', 'axylo-tooltip');\n   126\t  tooltip.hidden = true;\n   127\t  tooltip.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');\n   128\t  const readout = make('div', 'axylo-readout');\n   129\t  readout.hidden = true;\n   130\t  readout.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');\n   131\t  const controls = make('div', 'axylo-controls');\n   132\t  controls.hidden = true;\n   133\t  const top = make('div', 'axylo-controls axylo-controls-top');\n   134\t  top.hidden = true;\n   135\t  const side = make('div', 'axylo-controls axylo-controls-side');\n   136\t  side.hidden = true;\n   137\t  const body = make('div', 'axylo-body');\n   258\t\n   259\t### M0. Foundations (ceiling: 5 days)\n   260\t\n   261\t- Repository, build, test runners, CI matrix.\n   262\t- Public declarations generated from source and matching [docs/api/axylo.d.ts](api/axylo.d.ts); the examples file compiles in CI.\n   263\t- The acceptance matrix as data, every row \"not yet\", with applicability decided per chart type.\n   264\t- The benchmark harness from the performance plan, section 3: readiness markers, main-thread accounting, the reference-machine record, and adapters for uPlot and Chart.js. It measures those two before any Axylo code exists.\n   265\t\n   266\tOutcomes: `npm test` and `npm run build` pass on three operating systems; the API report is committed; the benchmark harness reproduces a uPlot and a Chart.js measurement with a recorded noise band.\n   267\t\n   268\t### M1. A vertical slice, and the two open decisions (ceiling: 12 days)\n   269\t\n   270\t- `line()` from rows and from typed columns: normalization with provenance, linear, time and date scales, DOM tick labels, resize, light and dark, `destroy`.\n   271\t- A minimal tooltip and one keyboard path, enough to exercise lookup and focus end to end.\n   272\t- **Renderer comparison:** the mark renderer built twice (Canvas 2D and SVG paths) behind the same scene, measured as in 2.3.\n   273\t- **Screen-reader pattern spike:** three candidates on the `trend` chart (application region with a live region; a roving labelled proxy; an adjustable control with value text), rehearsed on the five reader and browser pairs.\n   274\t- First measurements of P1, P2 and P5 with the accessibility layer present.\n   275\t\n   276\tOutcomes:\n   277\t- `trend` renders in three engines at 720 and 340 px; scene snapshot; resize in both directions with no call from the page.\n   278\t- 1,000 create–destroy cycles show no heap growth trend and no remaining listeners or observers.\n   279\t- Two written decision records, each with its measurements: the renderer, and the plot's interaction pattern. Each says what was observed and what was inferred.\n   280\t- Provisional budgets P1, P2, P5 and the size targets are recalibrated from the slice and recorded.\n   281\t\n   282\tExample: \"Line chart from an API response\". Docs: Getting started, Dat